<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scottish Reformation Parliament</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Reformation Parliament of 1560</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Scottish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> Parliament met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> in August 1560, after the Treaty of Edinburgh had removed French and English troops. Without the consent of the absent Mary, Queen of Scots, it abolished the pope's authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, forbade the celebration of Mass and adopted the Scots Confession of faith drafted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-knox">John Knox</a> and others, establishing Scotland as a Protestant kingdom.</p></div>
